","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Package installation, LDAP configuration, ACL changes, importing the staged data, and retaining a root-only administrator credential all directly supported the task. The transient authenticated test attributes were removed. The failed initial delete/import attempt made no observed change because authentication failed (cmd-affa68e59ba0439b), and setting the correct root password was the necessary corrective action. Restart scheduling and reboots served the mandatory evidence protocol; diagnostic polling was read-only. Both nodes have clean package state and no failed services. Restart evidence is complete and lifecycle-confirmed: each node had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, a changed boot ID, and recovered service/data behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-92ed3cad5e0e4132","cmd-7d9c537d192b4e3c","cmd-affa68e59ba0439b","cmd-8a233c941e8a44a1","cmd-6a5ac8de50cb4fe4","cmd-3bd9b4aa00704ad5","cmd-7815f3e69f5341d0","cmd-98419164972c4640","cmd-1d3ffbaac5c44cf7","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence. Node1 serves the imported directory, node2 finds both supplied users, write authorization behaves as required, and the OS and kernel were preserved. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes with verified recovery.","limitations":[]}
